{"transcript":"ˈdɪktə","exists":true,"definitions":["Authoritative pronouncements or statements.","Observations or remarks made by a judge in an opinion that are not essential to the decision of the case and therefore not binding as precedent."],"examples":["The judge's dicta were persuasive.","Legal scholars debated the dicta.","The court's dicta provided guidance."],"lemma":"dictum","lemmaPos":"noun","synonyms":["pronouncements","statements","rulings","observations"],"number":"plural","pluralForm":"dicta","source":"dicta"}